      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Prop Sheet\n\nOne **prop reference**: a single object on a clean seamless background, for an object that is held, recurs or carries the story.\n\n1. Rewrite **Prop (change me)**: silhouette, real-world size, materials, two to four identifying details, and the state (open or closed, lit or unlit).\n2. Match **Background** to the object: white, or gray when the object is white, silver, chrome or clear.\n3. Run, then check **Save Image**.\n\n**Three-panel sheet.** For a large or mechanical object, replace **Composition** with: *Three panels side by side in one horizontal row with even spacing: left, the whole object in a front three-quarter view; center, a full side profile; right, a close-up of [detail]. Same object, scale and lighting in every panel.* Then use a 16:9 size in Seedream.\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Prop Sheet\n\nOne **prop reference**: a single object on a clean seamless background, for an object that is held, recurs or carries the story.\n\n1. Rewrite **Prop (change me)**: silhouette, real-world size, materials, two to four identifying details, and the state (open or closed, lit or unlit).\n2. Match **Background** to the object: white, or gray when the object is white, silver, chrome or clear.\n3. Run, then check **Save Image**.\n\n**Three-panel sheet.** For a large or mechanical object, replace **Composition** with: *Three panels side by side in one horizontal row with even spacing: left, the whole object in a front three-quarter view; center, a full side profile; right, a close-up of [detail]. Same object, scale and lighting in every panel.* Then use a 16:9 size in Seedream.\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
